course: dictionary
lesson: 3875
title: Frazzled: words for being worn out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to everyday, chatty talk rather than formal writing. Frazzle is one of them, and you will hear it at home, in the kitchen and on busy days. The words around it give the clues. «When a parent seems frazzled after work, it is usually the workload, not anything the child did.» Workload means the amount of work someone has to do, so a frazzled parent has been worn down by too much work.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in your idea: «When a parent seems tired and stressed after work, it is usually the workload…» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: The same word can change meaning. In a kitchen, frazzle means burnt until black and crisp. Always read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
fact: Frazzle is an informal word, used in everyday talk.
fact: «Frazzled» means completely tired out, or tired, nervous and stressed.
fact: «To frazzle someone» means to make them tired, nervous and stressed.
fact: «Burnt to a frazzle» means burnt until black and crisp.
fact: Workload means the amount of work a person has to do.
exercise: When a parent seems «frazzled» after work, what does frazzled mean? | Cold and wet from the rain | Full of energy and ready to dance | Lost in the park | *Tired, nervous and stressed
exercise: What does «burnt to a frazzle» mean about the toast? | Cut into triangles | Covered in jam | *Burnt until black and crisp | Warm and soft
exercise: Which word in the sentence tells you the amount of work someone has to do? | child | *workload | seems | parent
test: Mum says, «Those kids have frazzled me today.» What does frazzled mean here? | Gave her a new job | *Made her tired and stressed | Fed her a big dinner | Made her laugh loudly
test: Which word is closest in meaning to frazzled when someone is completely tired out? | Relaxed | *Worn out | Excited | Curious
exam: Is frazzle a word for everyday chatty talk or a very formal word? | A word for the sea | *Everyday chatty talk | Very formal writing only | A word for numbers
